      "field_path": "regions.fl_peninsula.region_notes_seasoned",
      "our_prose": "In the Florida peninsula (zones 10 and 11), mint is an evergreen, year-round perennial; UF/IFAS reports it does well in Florida's hot, humid weather given part shade and moisture-retentive soil, so no heat pause is needed, though afternoon shade eases the peak of summer. Establish a contained plant, keep it evenly moist, and manage rust and leaf spot in the humidity by thinning, soil-line watering, and shearing. Contain the vigorous rhizomes.",
